<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__1683__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. ALABASTER" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Painters Colours and Pigments White Lead used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. ALABASTER"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The surface of alabaster may be etched by covering over the parts that are not to be touched with a solution of wax in oil of turpentine, thickened with white lead, and immersing the articles in pure water after the varnish has set."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
